b26e698625","event_uuid":"3b749afa-854e-4787-914f-3ef04c6e5a67","position":{"commit_sha":"28bca0f38448a9c95258354b903433cf9513c1de","position":"1795037384124906850-3b749afa-854e-4787-914f-3ef04c6e5a67"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"6457abf50c3ff026a43298fc65f7f4b8a16b907af4273a98621dc37440f678e9","event_uuid":"3f9ffdfa-73c9-4328-9cac-61595700df67","position":{"commit_sha":"7679766fcae0f68a781084e83203a2291619e59d","position":"1795037391953342091-3f9ffdfa-73c9-4328-9cac-61595700df67"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"fea08b2edffa617555864742ea9f64285fe795a115a39971e074de593eba2870","event_uuid":"a539f910-332a-46c8-a2f4-b4ddcb7208f2","position":{"commit_sha":"bacb7358f73b208cf02ebffb489ac8353186c4c6","position":"1795043228371382700-a539f910-332a-46c8-a2f4-b4ddcb7208f2"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"close_class":"preexisting","comments":[{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Measurement, 12 gate runs in one process (2026-11-18 PST). Each run calls rebar.llm.verify_completion(source=\"local\") on its own spawn_context_daemon thread (the MCP *_start shape), against an isolated scratch store, reaching Bedrock with dummy credentials (provider 403):\n- anyio 4.14.2 (current uv.lock): allocated blocks 636,038 -> 1,905,840; service-model OrderedDicts 18,444 -> 221,251. That is +115k blocks and +18,437 dicts per run, linear, with no levelling off. It is a leak, not a cache.\n- anyio 4.16.0 (same venv otherwise): blocks 565,674 -> 566,832 over 12 runs (flat, under 100 per run of noise); OrderedDicts constant at 7.\n- Single-variable confirmation in that venv: downgrading only anyio to 4.14.2 brings back +115k per run; 4.15.0 is flat.\nThe referrer chain is in the description. Fix: anyio>=4.15 floor plus re-lock (4.16.0). The new test fails on 4.14.2 (both the completed and raised drives) and passes on 4.16.0.","timestamp":1795028139820773295},{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Landed: Gerrit 3425 merged as 9ddb035cf598d27b80503a77afc30230f0666525 (LLM-Review +1, Verified +1). Local make verify passed: 21,395 default-tier and 226 integration tests. Portability: the change is a dependency floor plus a test that uses only threads, asyncio and weakref (no subprocess, fd, path, encoding or permission code), so the Windows sweep dispatch the rules require for that class of change does not apply.","timestamp":1795037234203015404}],"completion_expectation":"required","created_at":1794877266519759800,"creation_channel":"mcp","deps":[{"link_uuid":"9fde1f4e-a035-4d6e-bf43-7403df43f35f","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"e152-4009-4180-4fd8"},{"link_uuid":"11c03481-ab47-46d1-8945-13ae2380c03f","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"fd4b-9300-f0c0-4ee2"},{"link_uuid":"a539f910-332a-46c8-a2f4-b4ddcb7208f2","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"6ffc-a74b-dd65-4358"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\nEach MCP gate run leaves about 115k allocated blocks alive (18,437 botocore service-model `OrderedDict`s per run). Measured 2026-11-18 PST in an isolated scratch store, 12 `verify_completion` runs in one process, each on its own daemon thread (the MCP `*_start` shape), Bedrock reached with dummy credentials (provider returns 403): blocks grew 636,038 -> 1,905,840 linearly (+115k per run) and service-model `OrderedDict`s grew 18,444 -> 221,251 (+18,437 per run). Growth does not level off: it is a per-run leak, not a bounded cache.\n\n## Root cause (evidence)\nA breadth-first reachability search from `sys.modules` to a retained service-model dict found this chain:\n`anyio.lowlevel._run_vars` (WeakKeyDictionary keyed by event loop) -> per-loop RunVar dict -> `_root_task` -> asyncio `Task` -> its exception's traceback frame -> `BedrockConverseModel` -> `BedrockProvider` -> botocore `BedrockRuntime` client -> botocore `Loader` cache -> service-model dicts.\nanyio's `find_root_task()` caches the root task in a RunVar keyed by the loop; the task references the loop, so the weak key never dies and every per-run event loop (rebar creates one per gate thread via `ensure_current_event_loop`, and pydantic-ai's sync run reaches `anyio.to_thread.run_sync`) is retained with everything its task references. This is upstream anyio issue agronholm/anyio#1203, fixed in anyio 4.15.0. `uv.lock` pins anyio 4.14.2, which the MCP image installs (`uv sync --locked`).\nSingle-variable check in one venv: anyio 4.14.2 -> +115k blocks and +18.5k OrderedDicts per run; anyio 4.15.0 -> flat (543,052 -> 544,109 blocks over 4 runs, 7 OrderedDicts). No live botocore Session survives in either case; the retention is through the loop, not a session cache.\n\n## Approach\nRaise anyio to the fixed release rather than work around it in rebar (the documented upstream workaround, clearing the private `anyio.lowlevel._run_vars`, binds to anyio internals). Declare an `anyio>=4.15` floor in the `agents` and `mcp` extras (both run event loops through anyio), with a comment naming the upstream issue, so non-lock installs and the lowest-direct CI leg also get the fix; re-lock with `uv lock --upgrade-package anyio` so the lock moves only anyio. No config key, env var or flag.\n\n## Scope\n- `pyproject.toml` — anyio floor in `agents` and `mcp` extras.\n- `uv.lock` — anyio 4.14.2 -> 4.15.0 or later only.\n- `tests/unit/test_model_classes.py` — regression test.\n\n## Testing\n- New test: on a fresh thread, `ensure_current_event_loop()` drives a coroutine that awaits `anyio.to_thread.run_sync`, then closes and unsets the loop; after `gc.collect()` a weakref to that loop must be dead. Verified in scratch: fails on anyio 4.14.2 (loop retained), passes on 4.15.0.\n- Failure path: the same test with the drive raising inside the coroutine (the 403 shape) must also leave the loop collectable.\n- Portability: the test uses only threads, asyncio and weakref; no POSIX-only API.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [x] The owner of retained per-run objects is recorded on this ticket with the referrer chain (done in this description: anyio `_run_vars` root-task RunVar -> Task -> traceback -> Bedrock client).\n- [x] Per-run growth is removed, measured over at least 10 gate runs in one process: the scratch measurement shows flat allocated blocks with anyio at or above 4.15.0, recorded as a comment.\n- [x] `uv.lock` resolves anyio at or above 4.15.0 and `pyproject.toml` declares that floor in the `agents` and `mcp` extras.\n- [x] `tests/unit/test_model_classes.py` contains a test that fails on anyio 4.14.2 and passes on the locked version, for both a successful and a raising drive.\n- [x] `make verify` passes.","env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","file_impact":[{"path":"pyproject.toml","reason":"anyio>=4.15 floor in agents and mcp extras"},{"path":"uv.lock","reason":"move anyio 4.14.2 to the fixed release"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_model_classes.py","reason":"regression test: per-run event loop is collectable"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","managed_refs":[["relates_to","6ffc-a74b-dd65-4358"],["relates_to","fd4b-9300-f0c0-4ee2"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"3b749afa-854e-4787-914f-3ef04c6e5a67","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":3,"releases":[],"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"closed","tags":["mcp"],"ticket_id":"e266-c398-f5cd-4a3c","ticket_type":"bug","title":"Each MCP gate run leaves about 100k Python objects (botocore service-model data) alive after it finishes","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["dbf72ae4-bab6-4a80-b7a1-1b5a5ecaaf49","521819fc-d909-4a8e-9ac7-275e33264c02","f88776a1-8c02-4772-a99b-a03c170172df","430c4919-4f70-4b9d-807d-e328656ee045","260906cf-f27b-462a-8d51-4954ec35134a","e554ddb6-3a20-469f-8ca0-53efb29a5336","11c03481-ab47-46d1-8945-13ae2380c03f","b3fbda63-4cdf-42c0-ac63-b62788f7f37a","6ba6c1e4-5812-49d4-8fb2-6f2c4a3ba38b","dfe3c81f-6a0d-468d-9fea-7f494e1aa820","3b749afa-854e-4787-914f-3ef04c6e5a67","3f9ffdfa-73c9-4328-9cac-61595700df67","a539f910-332a-46c8-a2f4-b4ddcb7208f2"]},"env_id":"","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1795043228371382701,"uuid":"bc5bd0e9-eee0-4274-a12f-57db7362ea1a"}